WEBVTT

00:01.890 --> 00:05.700
Fortunately, Lord Braun's injuries are light.

00:05.700 --> 00:10.260
He wishes to hold the signing 
ceremony as soon as he recovers.

00:10.260 --> 00:13.190
Tell me, did he see his attacker?

00:13.810 --> 00:18.560
No, the villain hid himself 
under a hooded robe.

00:18.560 --> 00:25.010
But he was a young man, somewhat taller 
than Lord Braun, and he hid one eye.

00:25.240 --> 00:30.740
His Lordship resisted and tore out 
a tuft of his assailant's fur,

00:30.740 --> 00:33.900
but its color proved to be unremarkable.

00:34.540 --> 00:36.970
It will be difficult to 
identify him by sight, then.

00:36.970 --> 00:39.420
How in the world did he get in?

00:39.750 --> 00:41.430
What were the guards doing?

00:41.430 --> 00:44.020
Explain this failure, Captain Teiryn!

00:44.020 --> 00:45.670
Sir, I beg your—

00:45.670 --> 00:46.890
Please wait!

00:48.400 --> 00:52.190
We believe that we can name the culprit.

00:52.190 --> 00:53.200
What?!

00:56.530 --> 00:59.120
What's all this fuss 
first thing in the morning?

01:01.460 --> 01:04.630
Lante, where have you been?

01:04.630 --> 01:06.840
Oh, well, you know.

01:06.840 --> 01:10.860
There you have it. This man was 
nowhere to be seen last night.

01:10.860 --> 01:11.800
Huh?

01:11.800 --> 01:17.120
Captain Lanteveldt of the Queen's Guard 
is your man. I'm certain of it.

01:17.740 --> 01:18.330
Huh?

01:18.330 --> 01:19.280
What?!

02:51.020 --> 02:56.030
A False Charge and a Lonely Hyena

03:01.580 --> 03:03.580
So this is our culprit?

03:04.120 --> 03:07.040
Hold up. What are you talking about?

03:07.040 --> 03:10.540
His Lordship <i>did</i> mention 
that the man hid one eye...

03:10.760 --> 03:16.250
And he was already inside, so he 
wouldn't need to breach security.

03:16.250 --> 03:19.880
Then he really is Lord Braun's assailant?!

03:20.410 --> 03:21.440
Huh?

03:22.080 --> 03:25.000
You think I tried to assassinate the old fart?

03:26.250 --> 03:28.730
Gimme a break. That's ridiculous.

03:28.730 --> 03:30.720
What shameless conduct.

03:30.720 --> 03:34.060
Tell me, then: where were you all night, 
and what were you doing?

03:35.100 --> 03:39.080
Well, I didn't feel like running into anyone,

03:39.610 --> 03:42.450
so I kind of zoned out on 
top of this assembly hall.

03:42.450 --> 03:44.160
An obvious falsehood!

03:44.160 --> 03:45.130
Huh?

03:45.130 --> 03:46.420
Suspicious.

03:46.420 --> 03:48.040
Speak the truth!

03:50.420 --> 03:53.320
Hey! I told you I don't know anything!

03:53.320 --> 03:54.880
Quit hassling me, and—

04:00.710 --> 04:02.490
Arrest this man!

04:08.480 --> 04:10.610
Lante told you that he doesn't know anything!

04:11.130 --> 04:15.560
So he's innocent. And I'll prove it.

04:15.560 --> 04:17.350
Wh-What?!

04:18.550 --> 04:22.850
Acting Queen, do you mean to say 
that <i>you</i> will apprehend the culprit?

04:22.850 --> 04:27.660
She could just frame someone 
to escape responsibility!

04:27.660 --> 04:32.180
In that case, I shall accompany her.

04:33.480 --> 04:36.590
I bear responsibility for 
allowing this crime to occur.

04:37.490 --> 04:41.450
I must see it resolved before 
the ceremony tomorrow morning.

04:41.970 --> 04:43.730
<i>Before tomorrow morning...</i>

04:44.300 --> 04:47.410
But until the captain is cleared of suspicion,

04:47.410 --> 04:50.620
I must insist that he remain under guard.

04:50.620 --> 04:51.520
Hey!

04:52.790 --> 04:54.240
Let go of me!

04:54.240 --> 04:54.800
Lante.

04:56.600 --> 04:58.980
I believe in you, Lante.

04:59.280 --> 05:01.930
So believe in me, too, and wait.

05:07.080 --> 05:08.310
<i>Why...</i>

05:10.600 --> 05:13.020
Why do you trust him so completely?

05:13.020 --> 05:15.170
Because he's the captain of my guard!

05:15.750 --> 05:18.500
But I hear he was the only volunteer,

05:18.500 --> 05:23.580
and that he endangered your 
whole group on the journey here.

05:23.580 --> 05:29.250
He promised me that he wouldn't put 
other people in harm's way again.

05:29.810 --> 05:34.850
It is unwise to believe 
everyone you meet so blindly.

05:37.230 --> 05:43.400
Even I've met people I couldn't trust.

05:44.490 --> 05:49.260
But my gut tells me Lante isn't 
one of them, and I believe it.

05:50.080 --> 05:51.180
<i>Because...</i>

05:52.030 --> 05:56.260
Let Sariphi choose her own guard captain.

05:57.020 --> 05:59.590
<i>...that's part of trusting His Majesty.</i>

06:02.920 --> 06:05.720
Personally, I can't stand you.

06:06.210 --> 06:11.960
But Sari is running around to help you. 
I can see her through Cy's eye.

06:13.070 --> 06:18.190
Sari really does believe in you.

06:19.570 --> 06:20.650
So...

06:22.130 --> 06:24.450
you ought to trust her, too.

06:26.040 --> 06:28.800
<i>Why? I don't get it.</i>

06:29.540 --> 06:32.590
<i>She's... not normal.</i>

06:34.960 --> 06:38.230
<i>No one's ever covered 
for me like that before.</i>

06:39.890 --> 06:41.220
<i>Not even back then.</i>

06:42.410 --> 06:46.850
Hang on, Mom! I promise 
I'll buy you medicine!

06:48.960 --> 06:54.020
<i>A long time ago, we Hyenians turned 
traitor and sided against the king,</i>

06:54.020 --> 06:58.320
<i>so we're forced to live apart 
in our autonomous district.</i>

06:58.570 --> 07:03.860
<i>One step outside, and everyone 
looks down on us as traitors.</i>

07:03.860 --> 07:05.270
There he is again.

07:05.270 --> 07:08.980
Oh, dear. A Hyenian outside their district?

07:08.980 --> 07:11.400
He might have come to steal something.

07:12.490 --> 07:18.250
<i>But the other Hyenians called me 
and Mom traitors, too, and cut us off.</i>

07:19.410 --> 07:24.420
<i>All because Mom had me with 
a man from outside the district.</i>

07:27.920 --> 07:31.420
<i>Hyenians get almost no help from the 
kingdom, and we're even more isolated.</i>

07:31.420 --> 07:37.470
<i>So now my mom's dying of a disease 
that medicine could cure in no time.</i>

07:38.550 --> 07:40.080
Hang in there, Mom!

07:41.320 --> 07:43.970
I finally saved up enough from working!

07:44.550 --> 07:46.770
I'll buy you medicine right away!

07:47.960 --> 07:49.680
Mister! Gimme some medicine!

07:50.060 --> 07:51.840
My mom's sick!

07:52.440 --> 07:55.780
You'd better be able to pay for it.

07:56.470 --> 07:58.360
'Course I can! Look!

07:58.630 --> 08:01.140
Is this enough? Come on, hurry up!

08:07.380 --> 08:08.410
Do I need more?

08:14.150 --> 08:16.510
Here, take it.

08:18.360 --> 08:21.630
Have her take it slowly, a third at a time.

08:21.630 --> 08:23.180
Don't drop it, now.

08:23.180 --> 08:25.130
I won't! Thanks, mister!

08:29.610 --> 08:30.760
Stop right there!

08:30.760 --> 08:31.350
Huh?

08:31.690 --> 08:33.660
Is that medicine you're holding?

08:33.660 --> 08:38.280
A kid's allowance wouldn't cover that. 
How did you get it?

08:38.690 --> 08:41.360
W-Well, I went and...

08:41.360 --> 08:43.790
Sounds fishy. Did you steal it?

08:44.750 --> 08:47.390
No! I paid for it!

08:47.390 --> 08:49.770
I worked and bought it with my pay!

08:49.770 --> 08:52.360
<i>You</i>? Don't lie!

08:52.360 --> 08:55.990
I'm not lying! Ask the medicine seller!

08:56.320 --> 08:58.730
It's true! You've gotta believe me!

08:58.730 --> 09:02.110
Who'd believe a Hyenian?

09:02.110 --> 09:03.830
What? But...

09:04.320 --> 09:05.350
Come on!

09:05.350 --> 09:07.780
I always thought he seemed shifty.

09:07.780 --> 09:10.510
This explains the wares I lost the other day.

09:10.510 --> 09:15.270
Proud soldiers of Ozmargo would 
never accuse a child without cause.

09:18.140 --> 09:19.980
I'm confiscating this.

09:19.980 --> 09:22.140
Give it back! That's mine!

09:22.140 --> 09:23.070
Give it back!

09:24.280 --> 09:25.120
You little...

09:28.980 --> 09:29.960
Give it back.

09:30.340 --> 09:31.790
Give it back!

09:32.420 --> 09:34.820
I need that! Or my mom...

09:34.820 --> 09:37.300
My mom... My mom...

09:37.940 --> 09:41.250
My mom will die!

09:49.330 --> 09:53.710
<i>Why didn't anyone believe me?</i>

09:54.730 --> 09:58.360
<i>Because I'm a kid? Because I'm a Hyenian?</i>

10:00.250 --> 10:01.300
<i>No.</i>

10:02.860 --> 10:05.960
<i>Because they outranked me.</i>

10:06.630 --> 10:09.540
<i>Everyone believes big shots.</i>

10:10.040 --> 10:13.100
<i>Of course they do. That's normal.</i>

10:13.650 --> 10:15.960
<i>No one would trust a word I—</i>

10:17.530 --> 10:19.300
I believe in you.

10:23.870 --> 10:27.270
I'd say people like you are 
the least trustworthy of all.

10:27.580 --> 10:32.250
And since I can lie with a straight face, 
you'd be smart not to trust me much.

10:33.180 --> 10:34.360
<i>I knew it.</i>

10:35.770 --> 10:38.240
<i>I'm a big, fat liar.</i>

10:38.790 --> 10:43.140
<i>The truth is, I always wanted 
someone to trust me.</i>

10:44.170 --> 10:50.050
<i>To trust </i>me<i>, even if I'm 
some nobody Hyenian kid.</i>

10:52.290 --> 10:55.750
<i>Someone like you, Sariphi.</i>

11:05.180 --> 11:06.650
O-Oh, no!

11:06.650 --> 11:09.490
Hey! Bad news! We're out of ti—

11:10.190 --> 11:11.110
Huh?

11:15.340 --> 11:16.500
Lante...

11:19.500 --> 11:20.670
Get out.

11:20.670 --> 11:22.940
You've been exonerated.

11:27.460 --> 11:31.420
The culprit was a Badgerian 
youth named Nagma.

11:31.420 --> 11:34.330
His appearance tallies with 
Lord Braun's account,

11:34.810 --> 11:37.240
and he has confessed to the crime.

11:37.240 --> 11:40.810
How in the world did you 
find him, Captain Teiryn?

11:40.810 --> 11:43.740
That was the acting queen consort's doing.

11:43.740 --> 11:44.890
Sari!

11:45.940 --> 11:47.720
Lante! Clops!

11:47.720 --> 11:49.250
Sari!

11:50.090 --> 11:52.740
I'm so glad they let you go!

11:54.470 --> 11:58.080
How did you catch the real attacker, Sari?!

11:58.080 --> 12:00.030
Well, actually,

12:00.030 --> 12:01.870
I went by this.

12:04.440 --> 12:07.450
The fur taken as evidence!

12:07.940 --> 12:12.400
To me, this color looks completely 
different from Lante's fur.

12:12.400 --> 12:13.300
What?!

12:13.300 --> 12:14.540
I beg your pardon?!

12:15.060 --> 12:22.560
It seems the acting queen, being human, 
can distinguish colors that we cannot.

12:22.560 --> 12:24.220
P-Preposterous!

12:24.220 --> 12:28.250
Human eyes could not possibly 
be superior to ours!

12:28.250 --> 12:30.780
This is not a question of superiority.

12:30.780 --> 12:34.240
In any case, we had nothing else to go on,

12:35.530 --> 12:40.720
so I asked the acting queen to find someone 
whose fur matched in her eyes.

12:41.850 --> 12:46.080
I then rounded up members of that species

12:47.820 --> 12:51.510
and found one who behaved suspiciously.

12:56.260 --> 13:01.560
As he confessed when questioned, 
I immediately escorted him here.

13:02.940 --> 13:09.260
A background investigation revealed 
a history of anti-monarchist protest,

13:09.260 --> 13:15.170
and he claims to have been promised a 
promotion for preventing this ceremony.

13:15.530 --> 13:17.340
Hmm... I see.

13:17.340 --> 13:19.890
At any rate, well done.

13:20.270 --> 13:28.330
Acting Queen, a thousand pardons for 
wrongly imprisoning your guard captain.

13:28.740 --> 13:32.210
You don't owe me an apology.

13:32.700 --> 13:37.300
But I would like the people who suspected 
Lante to tell him they're sorry.

13:39.240 --> 13:44.500
Naturally. I apologize once more 
for my men's disrespect.

13:45.010 --> 13:50.390
But at present, let us arrange the ceremony 
at once and resolve this matter.

13:50.990 --> 13:55.240
I realize you have not slept and must 
be tired, but would you make ready?

13:55.240 --> 13:56.950
Okay. I understand.

14:02.080 --> 14:03.680
Hurry, Sari.

14:03.680 --> 14:04.600
Hurry.

14:04.600 --> 14:05.360
I know.

14:08.260 --> 14:11.250
So you had a lead from the start.

14:11.820 --> 14:14.500
No wonder you could say all 
that about believing in me.

14:15.170 --> 14:17.480
That's not why I said it.

14:18.340 --> 14:23.220
But you're "lucky I'm human," right?

14:24.380 --> 14:25.840
<i>Damn.</i>

14:29.380 --> 14:31.630
<i>I knew she was a crafty one.</i>

14:33.020 --> 14:34.290
<i>I can't beat her.</i>

14:38.130 --> 14:42.650
Lord Braun Breuse, in the name of 
His Majesty, the king of Ozmargo,

14:42.650 --> 14:47.400
I appoint you to govern this city of Maasya.

14:52.600 --> 14:58.200
I, Braun Breuse, humbly 
accept this appointment.

15:09.530 --> 15:12.680
I hope that life in Maasya 
settles down after this.

15:13.390 --> 15:15.550
Thank you, too, Captain.

15:15.550 --> 15:19.430
I couldn't have cleared 
Lante's name without you.

15:19.430 --> 15:21.020
I did nothing of note.

15:21.900 --> 15:26.150
Why did you believe in evidence 
that only I could see?

15:27.320 --> 15:32.450
Well, partly because I had 
nothing else to go on.

15:33.370 --> 15:37.670
But when I saw a queen 
aiding a lowly subject,

15:37.670 --> 15:41.880
to say nothing of a human 
making every effort for a beast,

15:43.300 --> 15:47.030
it simply seemed like the right thing to do.

15:48.940 --> 15:53.300
Thank you. I hope I get to see you again.

15:53.530 --> 15:56.770
Unfortunately, that may not be possible.

15:56.770 --> 15:57.520
What?

15:57.930 --> 16:00.730
The culprit in this attack

16:00.730 --> 16:03.790
entered through a spot that 
should have been guarded.

16:04.150 --> 16:08.790
In other words, my men abandoned 
their posts without leave.

16:09.710 --> 16:14.560
And I suspect they cast blame 
on your guard to hide that fact.

16:15.970 --> 16:18.740
Failing to detect that was 
a grave failure on my part.

16:19.170 --> 16:22.020
I'll be demoted at best, and at worst...

16:24.350 --> 16:28.370
In any case, I cannot expect 
to retain my current position.

16:29.200 --> 16:30.550
Oh, no...

16:30.550 --> 16:32.170
Ridiculous.

16:32.170 --> 16:34.490
None of that was your fault.

16:35.950 --> 16:38.370
Are you gonna take the fall for your men?

16:39.040 --> 16:42.630
A commander's role is not 
to throw his weight around.

16:43.530 --> 16:46.330
This is what it means to be in authority.

16:48.770 --> 16:52.670
Okay. But I still want to see you again.

16:54.290 --> 16:56.410
So, until next time, Captain.

16:59.310 --> 17:02.330
Yes, until we meet again.

17:14.180 --> 17:16.150
Y'know, I...

17:18.080 --> 17:22.730
I'm gonna climb the ranks, 
then kick back and take it easy.

17:24.760 --> 17:26.240
That's what I always wanted.

17:26.950 --> 17:31.490
'Cause without clout, a guy like me 
would just get trampled underfoot.

17:33.770 --> 17:34.410
But...

17:39.310 --> 17:43.160
You believed in me. In my pride.

17:47.690 --> 17:54.330
Acting Queen Sariphi, Lanteveldt the 
Hyenian will never forget this debt.

17:55.580 --> 18:00.750
Henceforth, I pledge my life 
and my loyalty to you.

18:07.120 --> 18:08.770
And that was no lie.

18:10.550 --> 18:14.670
Of course it wasn't! I believe you, Lante!

18:31.000 --> 18:36.110
The acting queen consort and her 
party have returned from Maasya!

18:38.720 --> 18:41.100
What?! What happened on the road?!

18:44.750 --> 18:47.180
Are you okay, Sari?

18:49.570 --> 18:51.220
Oh, watch out!

18:55.530 --> 18:57.610
Sari! Sari!

18:55.530 --> 18:58.680
Sari, are you hurt?!

18:57.610 --> 19:00.950
Don't be so dramatic. She's only sleeping.

19:00.950 --> 19:02.350
Sari!

19:02.350 --> 19:03.560
Ri!

19:05.380 --> 19:09.650
As a precaution, I have sent 
Lady Sariphi to rest in the infirmary.

19:09.650 --> 19:16.720
And this is the man she chose to lead 
her Queen's Guard, Lanteveldt.

19:17.090 --> 19:19.920
Hyenian, are you?

19:21.520 --> 19:23.880
Yeah. Is that a problem?

19:24.980 --> 19:26.960
Remember your place!

19:26.960 --> 19:30.710
Don't worry. I won't stab you in the back.

19:30.710 --> 19:32.860
I don't care about you enough for that.

19:32.860 --> 19:36.020
You dare address His Majesty thus?!

19:36.020 --> 19:38.560
Man, you never shut up, do you?

19:39.530 --> 19:44.530
I'm the captain of the Queen's Guard. 
I don't even work for the king.

19:44.530 --> 19:46.830
Th-That's nonsense!

19:48.390 --> 19:51.490
<i>He's like the wench all over again!</i>

19:51.900 --> 19:56.150
As a citizen of this realm, swearing 
fealty to its king is your natural duty!

19:56.150 --> 19:58.220
That's so old-fashioned.

19:58.570 --> 20:01.500
You oughta at least choose 
your own master, too.

20:01.500 --> 20:02.820
Wh-What?!

20:02.820 --> 20:03.940
I—

20:10.950 --> 20:12.970
I... I beg your pardon.

20:15.420 --> 20:17.470
Lanteveldt, is it?

20:18.380 --> 20:19.730
Answer me one question.

20:19.730 --> 20:21.180
Wh-What is it?

20:21.970 --> 20:26.110
Do you take pride in your own blood?

20:28.390 --> 20:31.580
Are you testing me?

20:31.890 --> 20:36.530
Well, sorry, but I <i>am</i> proud to be Hyenian.

20:37.040 --> 20:40.060
No one hates themselves for who they are.

20:40.550 --> 20:44.300
They learn to hate themselves because 
other people mock and insult them.

20:45.210 --> 20:47.870
I don't wanna end up like that.

20:48.410 --> 20:52.260
Not even if you order me 
to give up my pride, sire.

20:53.740 --> 20:56.410
Sariphi's the only one who 
gets to boss me around.

20:56.980 --> 21:00.930
She's the only person my heart will listen to.

21:05.080 --> 21:07.290
Very well, Lanteveldt.

21:07.920 --> 21:12.780
I hereby ratify you as captain of 
my acting queen's personal guard.

21:13.440 --> 21:19.260
Become her knight—her sword 
and shield—in title and in truth.

21:20.230 --> 21:21.610
Now, leave us.

21:21.610 --> 21:22.300
Yes, sire.

21:33.910 --> 21:37.000
<i>Me, a knight?</i>

21:42.370 --> 21:45.190
<i>All right. Why not?</i>

21:47.050 --> 21:48.400
<i>I'll do it.</i>

23:25.960 --> 23:28.260
One, two...

23:28.260 --> 23:31.100
Why are you counting plates, Amit?

23:32.420 --> 23:35.840
They're flowers. This is a traditional 
Murgan method of foretelling romance.

23:35.840 --> 23:39.480
I pray that he returns safe and sound.

23:37.020 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode

23:37.020 --> 23:40.010
Chance Meeting of a Boy and a Child
